'','**These are approximate model coordinates, not camera-calibrated anatomical angles.** Pitch/yaw coupling, roll and model error can move a photograph in the scatterplot. Iris position relative to eye corners is recorded separately as a gaze proxy, never substituted for head yaw. Blendshape blink scores and eyelid ratios identify screening candidates; side-eye occlusion and downward iris hiding can be misclassified as blinks. The visual review supplements missed partial blinks and explicitly distinguishes deep-bow occlusion.',
'','Per-frame records include yaw/pitch/roll, iris proxies, eyelid openness, blink, smile/jaw blendshapes, face scale, nose translation, key landmarks, face Laplacian sharpness, background intensity/change, collar change and local hair/beard/shoulder temporal differences. Anatomical quality and identity are photographic judgments, not facts proved by those proxies. No biometric identity embedding was used. Every frame was reviewed at contact size; subtle native-pixel identity/texture invariance is **not certified**. This limitation strengthens the decision to avoid runtime approval.',
