'','## Extraction and resource management','',f"The pre-extraction estimate was 2.08 GB of high-quality JPEGs plus a 500 MB lossless shortlist budget, against about 257.6 GB free. Actual native JPEG storage is **{sum(v['extracted_bytes'] for v in inv)/1e6:.2f} MB**. Extraction was sequential, FFmpeg JPEG quality 1, with no resolution reduction and no FPS resampling. Frames are named `data/extracted/<original-stem>/frame_000000.jpg` onwards. Each extracted sequence matches its original decoded count and dimensions. Timestamps equal n/24 within 10 microseconds; s07 ends at n238, not an invented n239.",
'','Lossless PNG references for 14 shortlisted photographs were decoded directly from the MP4, not converted from an already-lossy JPEG. Source-video compression remains authoritative; PNG cannot recover detail absent from the source. Pose detection processes one image at a time. Graph analysis retains 240×135 audit thumbnails (422.61 MiB), not full-resolution decoded photographs. No browser texture atlas is preloaded.',
