'## Pose surface, interior gaps and adjacency','',
'![Source-colored pose coverage](scatterplot.png)','![Screened pose density](density.png)','![Interior coverage gaps](gaps.png)','![Compatibility screening graph](compatibility-graph.png)','',
f"The screening graph contains **{summary['graph_edges']:,} provisional edges**, including **{summary['cross_source_edges']} cross-source edges**, and **{summary['components']} connected components**. Candidates include eight nearest angular neighbors, original adjacent frames, the known V15 frame 0→8 bridge, and every transition selected by the four circle diagnostics. An edge requires <=2.5° approximate pose separation, <=5 px RMS raw landmark displacement at 960×540, <=2° roll change, <=3% scale difference, <=0.065 gaze proxy difference, <=0.15 smile difference, registered-face MAE <=8, collar/shoulder MAE <=4, hair MAE <=10, beard MAE <=12 and background MAE <=3 on 0–255 channels. These thresholds are explicit screening choices, not perceptual laws. Smile and beard limits were relaxed against the known V15 sequence: all **48/48** selected baseline transitions now pass. The V15 sample maximum beard MAE was 11.77 and maximum smile-score delta 0.141. The graph therefore accepts the known good baseline.",
'','Registration is a partial affine comparison computed from tracked landmarks. It removes some translation/scale/rotation for face-texture comparison while raw displacement remains an independent rejection criterion. It does not create a new face image for runtime. A graph edge that passes the screen remains provisional; identity and naturalness require photographic verification. The graph searches a finite candidate neighborhood, not every possible pair. Component count is therefore method-dependent and is not alone proof of impossibility.',
'',f"The largest provisional component has {summary['largest_components'][0]['count']} frames and spans yaw {summary['largest_components'][0]['yaw'][0]:.2f}…{summary['largest_components'][0]['yaw'][1]:.2f} and pitch {summary['largest_components'][0]['pitch'][0]:.2f}…{summary['largest_components'][0]['pitch'][1]:.2f}. Its bounding box is **not a filled rectangle**. It connects several thin directional branches; remaining rightward holds and rolled/upper sections fragment further. Graph connectivity alone would permit long detours through irrelevant poses, which would misrepresent a requested cursor path. Cross-source edges remain photographic candidates, not approved identity-preserving transitions.",
